+@ (the label keeps Wallace's name: it is the one the object points to) Talking to Birch: "Show me what you've got", the battle,
+@ then nothing more: the professor has the last word inside the battle, the result is written when that text is done (battle_main.c),
+@ and the room does not come back.
 EverGrandeCity_ChampionsRoom_EventScript_Wallace::
-	playbgm MUS_ENCOUNTER_CHAMPION, FALSE
-	msgbox EverGrandeCity_ChampionsRoom_Text_IntroSpeech, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
-	trainerbattle_no_intro TRAINER_WALLACE, EverGrandeCity_ChampionsRoom_Text_Defeat
-	goto EverGrandeCity_ChampionsRoom_EventScript_Defeated
-	end
+	lockall
+	msgbox Oakle_Text_ShowMe, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
+	trainerbattle_no_intro TRAINER_BIRCH_1, Oakle_Text_Defeat
+	end @ the battle is the end: its last text and the result are handled in battle_main.c, and the room does not come back
